  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Plage des Marines de Cogolin offers 400 metres of sand and a wide panorama over the Gulf of Saint-Tropez, with the municipal water-sports base. This listing covers the Cogolin side of the beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The town hall has regulated dog access ("Plage des Marines de Cogolin, summer 2026"): order no. 2026/634 bans dogs from the beach, even on a leash, from 1am to 7pm from Monday 15 June to Thursday 15 October 2026. From 7pm to 1am, the beach is open to dogs on a leash, except guard and attack dogs (category 2). Dogs are banned, even on a leash, in the designated swimming area during this period. Walk your dog before arriving, as it is forbidden to let it defecate or urinate on the beach. For the rest of the year, the 2026 order is silent: ask the town hall. A paid "Toutou Douche" (€1 per minute) lets you rinse your dog.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this beach also extends onto the Gassin side under the name Plage de Bertaud; the rule above is Cogolin's, so check on site if you settle on the Gassin side.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The municipal water-sports base offers water activities year-round.</p>
